                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237185270",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561199077808024",
                            "num_reviews": 5,
                            "playtime_forever": 3958,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 624,
                            "playtime_at_review": 3333,
                            "last_played": 1793249939
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I don't know how to explain the tone of this game, it's Minecraft with an MMO bolted on and a shop attached to everything, like EA got their hands on a box of cubes.\n\nI put 50+ hours into building and leveling a class and grinding for endgame gems, and the game will happily let you skip all of it if you pay (so generous of them), and every time someone calls it pay to win a fan turns up to say it's only pay to progress, which is the same thing with a nicer name.\n\nI'd be having a great time wandering around the voxel world and suddenly I hit the time-gated gem grind with the servers rubberbanding.\n\nAnyway, 6/10, free to play and expensive to skip.",
